<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss producer/import prices rise 0.2 pct in Jan.</title>
<headline>Swiss producer/import prices rise 0.2 pct in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The combined index for Swiss producer and import prices rose 0.2 percent in January versus December, and was down 1.9 percent versus the previous year, the Federal Statistics Office (BfS) said.</p>
<p>The Swiss import price index alone rose in January versus December by 0.7 percent to an absolute index level of 96.0. On a year-on-year basis import prices were down 1.9 percent.</p>
<p>BfS said the increases in producer prices versus December was due to increased prices for citrus fruits, coffee, cocoa, eggs, meats and other foodstuffs, textile materials, petrol, diesel fuel, heating oil and coal.  </p>
<p>Price rises in imported goods were also seen in precious metals, aluminum, copper, lead, zinc and nickle.</p>
<p>Combined producer/import price index:</p>
<p>					Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 1996</p>
<p> Monthly pct change	     +0.2	+0.1	-0.1</p>
<p> Yearly pct change		-1.9	-2.2	-1.4</p>
<p> Index (100 = May 1993)	 96.6	96.5	98.5</p>
<p>Producer price index:</p>
<p>					Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p> Monthly pct index change	0.0	0.0	 0.0</p>
<p> Yearly pct index change	 -1.9     -1.9	-0.7</p>
<p> Index (100 = May 1993)	  96.9     96.9	98.7</p>
<p>Import price index:</p>
<p>					Jan 97    Dec 96    Jan 96</p>
<p> Monthly pct index change     +0.7	+0.3	-0.4</p>
<p> Yearly pct index change	-1.9	-2.9	-2.8</p>
<p> Index (100 = May 1993)	 96.0	95.3	97.8</p>
<p>	  -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
